Folds in Fable's design pass (routing → Now → card diet → board grouping), on v5 dd8b0867.

Routing (unlocks the rest):
- Entity hash routes #/issue/:id, #/epic/:id, #/decision/:id, #/work/:slug,
  #/board?epic=:id. The detail overlay is route-driven — opening sets the hash,
  browser Back closes it, entities are deep-linkable/shareable. Any text naming an
  entity is its link; a topbar breadcrumb shows the path (Epic › Task).
- Issue/epic detail = the hub: renders every link slot (parent epic, children, PR,
  worktree, work folder, files, comments) even when SEAM-tagged (56461780), so the
  graph shape is always visible.

One card everywhere:
- A single card component (status-or-pulse · title · owner — a strict 3-item budget)
  shared by board / epic grids / memory / search; epics add the same progress bar +
  done/total used in the detail. Phase stepper, type badge and 8-char id are retired
  from cards to the detail hub. Priority is a small P0–P4 label (fill square gone).

Board — one axis, epics as grouping:
- Status is the only spatial axis (Backlog → Ready → In progress + Done/Cancelled
  toggle). Deleted the Tasks/Epics level toggle and the epic-health columns. Epics
  are grouping headers inside each column (click → the epic's detail); focus one
  epic via #/board?epic=:id ("see on board" link in the epic detail).

Now (was Live Ops):
- Replaced the three parallel inventories with ONE joined list of active threads:
  one row per live claim (pulse · agent · issue title → branch · PR · age), a
  one-sentence header (N agents · M PRs · K needs you → Needs-Attention), and quiet
  secondary lists (open PRs, worktrees). Branch/PR↔issue join = honest SEAM. Only
  the pulse animates, one per row.

Visual language:
- Two-tier type: sans for titles/body, mono reserved for data; de-capped chrome
  titles so one caps-tracked tier (section labels) survives. Row lists use spacing,
  not inner borders (one frame deep). Glyph restraint (● ◐ ○ ✕ + pulse only).

Interaction-verified in-browser (fresh bundle): entity routing + Back-closes +
deep-link, card diet (74 unified cards, 0 legacy), epic grouping, Now joined list
(15 rows/15 pulses), filters, dark-default; 12 tests pass.

Refs Fable design pass on dc81d48d (v5). Routes: 56461780, a2279f65, 7dc229d4.

